Note that the `http-client` import goes beyond the node's current `with` clause. If the graph validator checks imports against the deployed graph definition, it may reject this component until the graph update ships.

The enrichment call uses `fetch` rather than `get`, so a down or slow endpoint is returned as a value and cannot fail the run. Its result is discarded, so the digest is computed exactly as before. The query text is the selected items' titles, percent-encoded and capped at 500 characters.

